  /*
    The work-index hover preview, shown on a monitor: the same 3px raster as
    the hero's CRT, static, over the cover. Static on purpose — the frame
    already moves with the pointer, and a rolling band inside a moving frame
    is two motions fighting.
  */
  .work-preview::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    pointer-events: none;
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      transparent 0 2px,
      rgb(0 0 0 / 0.2) 2px 3px
    );
  }

  /*
    The hero's CRT. The glitch on Technical / Roots is a TV losing signal; this
    is the TV. Values follow `.crt` in BreakoutCTA so the two read as the same
    tube, top of the page and bottom.

    - The raster is dark lines on a 3px pitch (2px moirés on fractional zoom,
      4px reads as stripes). Dark lines only register over something lit, so
      they show in the purple/blue wash and vanish on the black — which is the
      brief. A much fainter *light* raster, offset 1px into the gaps, gives the
      black some texture too, the same fix as RASTER in the CTA.
    - The mask follows the wash: strongest top-right, gone by the bottom-left
      corner where the headline and stats sit.
    - Two roll bands on clocks that share no factor (10.3s / 15.7s), so they
      drift in and out of phase rather than looping. Each band's translateY end
      is 100 / its height: 22% -> 455%, 9% -> 1111%. Change one, change both.
    - A faint stepped flicker on the whole layer (~0.9–1 opacity), the supply
      ripple an old set has even when the picture is fine.

    All transform/opacity on their own layers, so it composites and never
    repaints. Reduced motion keeps the raster (composition) and drops the bands
    and flicker (motion), same split as the CTA.
  */
  .hero-crt {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    pointer-events: none;
    background-image:
      repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 0 2px, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.22) 2px 3px),
      repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 0 1px, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.018) 1px 2px, transparent 2px 3px);
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(130% 120% at 100% 0%, #000 30%, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5) 62%, transparent 92%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(130% 120% at 100% 0%, #000 30%, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5) 62%, transparent 92%);
    animation: hero-crt-flicker 4.9s steps(1, end) infinite;
  }
  .hero-crt::before,
  .hero-crt::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: 0;
    top: 0;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  .hero-crt::after {
    height: 22%;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      transparent 0%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.022) 45%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.032) 60%,
      transparent 100%
    );
    animation: hero-crt-roll 10.3s linear infinite;
  }
  .hero-crt::before {
    height: 9%;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      transparent 0%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.02) 55%,
      transparent 100%
    );
    animation: hero-crt-roll-fast 15.7s linear infinite;
    animation-delay: -6s;
  }
  @keyframes hero-crt-roll {
    from { transform: translateY(-100%); }
    to { transform: translateY(455%); }
  }
  @keyframes hero-crt-roll-fast {
    from { transform: translateY(-100%); }
    to { transform: translateY(1111%); }
  }
  @keyframes hero-crt-flicker {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
    23% { opacity: 0.92; }
    23.6% { opacity: 1; }
    61% { opacity: 0.88; }
    61.4% { opacity: 0.97; }
    61.8% { opacity: 1; }
    84% { opacity: 0.94; }
    84.5% { opacity: 1; }
  }
